Your Task
Create a Solution Architecture Diagram (also known as a Component or C4-style Container Diagram) that shows the overall deployed structure of the security system

Your diagram must include the following components:

Web Dashboard: How users interact with the solution
API Gateway: The single entry point for client applications.
Device Ingestion Service: Responsible for receiving reported data from device sensors
Event Bus: The central nervous system for asynchronous communication.
Central Control Service: The core service that, among other things:
Consumes, validates, and transforms the data;
Adjusts lighting and A/C targets according to preconfigured values for given numbers of occupants;
Writes historical records out to storage.
Data Stores: Show at least two different types of databases (e.g., a relational DB for user accounts and a time-series DB for sensor data).
The diagram should clearly illustrate the primary communication paths between these components (e.g., showing which services talk to the API Gateway vs. which services communicate via the Event Bus).